Make codesigning and archive processing work under strict remote
execution.

Default codesign_inputs to //apple:sdk_tool_files so that codesigning
actions (ProcessAndSign, SignBinary, and bundletool-embedded signing)
declare the cross-toolchain's xcrun/codesign/zip binaries as inputs.
Local no-sandbox execution resolves them from the execroot either way,
but strict remote execution only stages declared inputs.

Also resolve relative PATH entries in the process-and-sign script before
it changes directories: the toolchain bin directory is provided as an
execroot-relative PATH entry, which stops resolving once the script
pushd's into the archive root to zip the bundle.

Also feed sdk_tool_files to every xcrun-based resource action (actool,
ibtool, momc, coremlc, copypng, TextureAtlas, metal, xcstringstool) via
resources_support, and export the calling tool's hermetic Python as
PYTHON3 so interpreter-less executor images can run python stub tools.

Also expose sdk_tool_files on AppleMacToolsToolchainInfo and feed them to
the SwiftStdlibCopy action, replacing its no-remote/no-sandbox opt-out:
with the tools declared as inputs the action can run remotely, which a
macOS host requires because the staged tool binaries are Linux
executables.

